      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While consistency is helpful, it's not a substitute for medical supervision. Vitamin K and warfarin can interact unpredictably, and even small changes in your vitamin K intake may significantly affect your warfarin levels. Irregular increases in vitamin K can lead to life-threatening blood clotting events, making it crucial to discuss your supplement usage with your doctor before making any changes to your routine.",
